  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a tree with NNN vertices numbered from 111 to NNN. Your goal is to handle QQQ queries. For each query you are given KKK nodes v1,v2,…,vKv_1, v_2, \\ldots, v_Kv1​,v2​,…,vK​. Find if there exists a simple path in the tree covering all the given vertices.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\leq T \\leq 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤u,v,vj≤N1 \\leq u, v, v_j \\leq N1≤u,v,vj​≤N",
      "1≤Q≤1051 \\leq Q \\leq 10^51≤Q≤105",
      "1≤Ki≤N1 \\leq K_i \\leq N1≤Ki​≤N for each valid iii.",
      "The edges form a valid tree.",
      "All vertices in a single query are distinct.",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105.",
      "For each test case, the sum of KiK_iKi​ over all queries does not exceed 10510^5105.",
      "SubtasksSample Input`1",
      "6",
      "1 2",
      "1 3",
      "2 4",
      "2 5",
      "3 6",
      "2",
      "3 6 2 4",
      "4 2 3 4 5",
      "`Sample Output`YES",
      "NO",
      "`ExplanationThe structure of the given tree is shown below.",
      "For the first query the path will be 4−2−1−3−64 - 2 - 1 - 3 - 64−2−1−3−6.",
      "For the second query there is no simple path that covers all the given vertices."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line contains a single integer TTT - the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nEach of the following N−1N-1N−1 lines contains two integers uuu and vvv denoting an edge between nodes uuu and vvv.\nThe next line contains a single integer QQQ - the number of queries.\nThe next QQQ lines describe queries. The iii-th line describes the iii-th query and starts with the integer KiK_iKi​ — the number of vertices in the current query. Then KiK_iKi​ integers follow: v1,v2,…,vKiv_1, v_2, \\ldots, v_{K_i}v1​,v2​,…,vKi​​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each query print `\"YES\"` (without quotes) if there exists a simple path in the tree covering all the given nodes, otherwise print `\"NO\"` (without quotes).\n\nYou may print each character of the string in uppercase or lowercase (for example, the strings `\"yEs\"`, `\"yes\"`, `\"Yes\"` and `\"YES\"` will all be treated as identical).",
    "notes": [],
